  "scenario": {
    "summary": "Guest opens a simple product's PDP, opens Write a Review, checks the review page labels and blank-field errors, submits a review (rating, headline, comment, name, location) and verifies it is listed under the product's reviews after a refresh.",
    "steps": [
      "Open the webstore, search the product SKU and open its PDP",
      "Open the Reviews tab and Write a Review",
      "Verify product name, review page labels and blank validation errors",
      "Fill rating, headline, review text, name and state/country; submit; close the confirmation",
      "Refresh the PDP, open Reviews and verify the new review"
    ],
    "entitiesTouched": [
      "store",
      "product",
      "review"
    ],
    "stateChanges": [
      "A product review is created for the product (stays; no teardown, as in the Playwright review entries)"
    ],
    "assertions": [
      "Review page shows the product name",
      "Labels 'Rating *', 'Review headline *', 'Review *', name, 'Your state/country*'",
      "Blank submit shows the five required-field errors",
      "Submitted review (headline, text, name, location) is listed on the PDP after refresh"
    ],
    "evidence": [
      "Independent method (no dependsOn); linkedCases Z10-TC-8412 and Z10-TC-8648 come from the scan (TestNG groups); Z10-TC-7853 is in the class comment.",
      "Key PRODUCT_SIMPLE_IN_STOCK (quantityUsed 1, nothing is added): any reviewable simple product; the Playwright review entries use the same key (2026-11-02: the review tab issue was framework, not data). The sheet product z-2420005 has a Required add-on, which this key excludes: the preferred record will not pass and the resolver falls back.",
      "The review values the test types (ReviewHeadline, ReviewComments, ReviewerUsername (masked), ReviewerCountry) are created by the test: created-by-test. The review shows at once only if the store publishes reviews without moderation (store setting, not a data need; unchanged from today).",
      "LabelUsername (masked by the key-name rule) is the name field label: expected-output, sensitive.",
      "ProductName (E3) -> product.name (review page product name).",
      "Store: openWebstoreUrl opens automation_webStoreUrl (atstage: webstore-z10-atstage, the main store MaxwellsHardware; centralizedLoginEnabled=no), the same store as the Playwright webstore entries. Guest flow, no sign-in (the CentralizedLogin group is a tag only; no login call in the method).",
      "Profile: work/profiles/profile.json (2026-11-01) was not run for these Selenium tests (profiled false); sheet SKUs were looked up read-only with bin/tda rows (2026-11-06) where cited.",
      "Scanned constant values (locators, report messages, map key prefixes) are framework constants: role config, no need.",
      "migrate: Selenium reads Excel tables through TestData.getMap / getHashMap; there is no swap for Selenium."
    ],
    "confidence": "medium"
  },
